species.duck.desc=Cheerful, chatty and never far from water. Ducks waddle about in a little line, dabble for weeds and preen until every feather sits just so.
species.duck.rare=Some say a duck with a ring of gold round its neck once came down to a quiet pond, though nobody has kept one yet.
behaviour.dabble.name=bottoms up
behaviour.dabble.note=Tips forward until only its tail points at the sky, dabbling for weeds.
behaviour.paddle.name=a lazy paddle
behaviour.paddle.note=Settles low and bobs about, feet paddling away out of sight.
behaviour.preen.name=a careful preen
behaviour.preen.note=Works through every wing feather with its bill until they shine.
behaviour.quack.name=a proud quack
behaviour.quack.note=Stretches its neck and quacks, just to let everyone know where it is.
species.camel.desc=Patient, proud and never in a hurry. Camels love warm sand and a long sit, and chew things over very carefully.
species.camel.rare=Desert travellers whisper of a camel as pale as moonlit dunes.
species.goat.desc=Nimble, nosy and fond of high places. Goats will climb anything, nibble everything and butt heads with their friends just for fun.
species.goat.rare=Mountain folk tell of a goat with a coat as dark as wet slate.
behaviour.cud_chew.name=a slow chew
behaviour.cud_chew.note=Folds down onto its knees and chews the cud for a good long while.
behaviour.spit_snort.name=a spit and snort
behaviour.spit_snort.note=Tosses its head with a grand snort. Best to stand to one side.
behaviour.rock_hop.name=a rock hop
behaviour.rock_hop.note=Springs up onto its hind legs whenever there is a rock to climb.
behaviour.headbutt.name=a friendly headbutt
behaviour.headbutt.note=Rears up and bumps heads with a friend. Nobody gets hurt, everybody has fun.
behaviour.bleat.name=a bleat
behaviour.bleat.note=Has a great deal to say, and says it loudly.
behaviour.browse.name=a nibble
behaviour.browse.note=Nibbles on leaves, twigs and anything else within reach.
species.rabbit.desc=Soft, twitchy and secretly very bold. Rabbits nibble their way across sunny meadows, and when they are truly happy they leap and twist in the air.
species.rabbit.rare=Some say a rabbit with a coat like fresh snow hops through clover where carrots grow.
species.mouse.desc=Tiny, tidy and always busy. Mice keep to cozy corners near a hay pile, wash their whiskers twice an hour and never turn down a crumb of cheese.
species.mouse.rare=Farmers whisper of a little golden mouse that only visits the fullest grain stores.
behaviour.binky.name=a binky
behaviour.binky.note=Leaps into the air with a twist and a kick. A rabbit only does this when it is very happy.
behaviour.burrow.name=a little burrow
behaviour.burrow.note=Scrabbles at soft earth with its front paws, as if a tunnel might be started today.
behaviour.thump.name=a thump
behaviour.thump.note=Sits up tall and thumps a hind foot on the ground to tell everyone something.
behaviour.ear_wash.name=an ear wash
behaviour.ear_wash.note=Sits up, washes its face, then pulls an ear down to give it a careful clean.
behaviour.scurry.name=a scurry
behaviour.scurry.note=Dashes off, stops dead to look around, then dashes back as if nothing happened.
behaviour.seed_nibble.name=a seed nibble
behaviour.seed_nibble.note=Sits up and turns a seed round and round in its paws while it nibbles.
behaviour.whisker_sniff.name=a whisker sniff
behaviour.whisker_sniff.note=Stands up on its hind legs and sniffs the air, whiskers going.
behaviour.face_wash.name=a face wash
behaviour.face_wash.note=Rubs its face and ears with both paws until it is perfectly tidy.
species.squirrel.desc=Quick, bright eyed and always busy. Squirrels dart between trees, sit up to nibble and hide nuts for later.
species.squirrel.rare=Some say a squirrel with a coat as dark as a winter night lives in the oldest woods.
species.crab.desc=A sideways walker with a brave pair of claws. Crabs love warm sand, cool water and anything shiny on the shore.
species.crab.rare=Sailors tell of a crab with a shell as blue as deep water.
behaviour.nibble.name=a nibble break
behaviour.nibble.note=Sits up on its haunches and nibbles a nut held in both paws.
behaviour.bury_nut.name=a buried nut
behaviour.bury_nut.note=Digs a little hole in the grass, tucks a nut inside and pats it down.
behaviour.tail_flick.name=a tail flick
behaviour.tail_flick.note=Flicks its big tail twice when something catches its eye.
behaviour.claw_wave.name=a claw wave
behaviour.claw_wave.note=Raises one claw high and waves it about, as if saying hello.
behaviour.sand_dig.name=a dig in the sand
behaviour.sand_dig.note=Wiggles down into soft sand until only its eyes show, then pops back up.
behaviour.bubble.name=a bubble break
behaviour.bubble.note=Sits still and froths little bubbles at its mouth.
behaviour.sidestep.name=a sideways shuffle
behaviour.sidestep.note=Scuttles left and right on the spot, claws held out for balance.
species.mosshorn.desc=A gentle forest giant wearing a coat of moss. Mosshorns browse the shady woods, nibble every mushroom they find and never hurry anywhere.
species.mosshorn.rare=Woodcutters tell of a mosshorn so old that ferns grow from its back.
species.turkey.desc=Proud, chatty and very fond of an audience. Turkeys strut about with their tails fanned and answer every sound with a gobble.
species.turkey.rare=Some say a turkey with a fan of pure white feathers struts the far meadows.
behaviour.moss_graze.name=a mossy graze
behaviour.moss_graze.note=Crops soft moss and ferns from the forest floor, slow and content.
behaviour.shake_moss.name=a good shake
behaviour.shake_moss.note=Shakes from horns to tail, and moss and twigs fly everywhere.
behaviour.antler_rub.name=an antler rub
behaviour.antler_rub.note=Leans on a tree trunk and rubs its antlers up and down, eyes half closed.
behaviour.mushroom_nibble.name=a mushroom nibble
behaviour.mushroom_nibble.note=Finds a mushroom and nibbles it very carefully, as if it were a treat.
behaviour.strut.name=a proud strut
behaviour.strut.note=Puffs up, fans its tail wide and turns slowly so everyone can admire it.
behaviour.gobble.name=a gobble
behaviour.gobble.note=Stretches out its neck and gobbles, wattle wobbling, at anything that makes a sound.
species.tortoise.desc=Slow, wise and very fond of the sun. A tortoise takes its time over everything, from a lettuce leaf to a long warm nap, and it will be your friend for a very long while.
species.tortoise.rare=Old ranchers tell of a tortoise with a shell like polished amber, older than any of them.
species.meerkat.desc=Curious little sentries that live in busy groups. One always stands up tall to keep watch while the others dig, chatter and pile up together for a cuddle.
species.meerkat.rare=Some say a meerkat with a coat as pale as moonlight keeps watch over the quietest dunes.
behaviour.bask.name=a sunbathe
behaviour.bask.note=Spreads out flat on warm ground, stretches its neck to the sky and closes its eyes.
behaviour.shell_tuck.name=a shell tuck
behaviour.shell_tuck.note=Pulls its head and legs into its shell, then peeks out slowly to see if all is well.
behaviour.leaf_munch.name=a slow munch
behaviour.leaf_munch.note=Lowers its head to the greens and chews, and chews, and chews.
behaviour.sentry.name=sentry duty
behaviour.sentry.note=Stands up tall on its hind legs and turns its head slowly from side to side, keeping watch.
behaviour.forage_dig.name=a little dig
behaviour.forage_dig.note=Scrabbles at the sand with both front paws, hunting for something tasty underneath.
behaviour.huddle.name=a huddle
behaviour.huddle.note=Curls up close to a friend, cheek to cheek, eyes half closed.
behaviour.chitter.name=a chitter
behaviour.chitter.note=Lifts its nose and chirps a quick string of little sounds to the rest of the group.
species.fox.desc=Clever, curious and full of mischief. A fox pounces into snow and tall grass after things only it can hear, curls up with its tail over its nose to sleep, and loves to bring you its latest treasure.
species.fox.rare=Some say a fox will bring the best thing it ever found to the one person it trusts most.
species.wolf.desc=Loyal to the end and happiest with its pack. Wolves trot together, bow to ask a friend to play, lie down to keep watch over home and lift their voices to the sky.
species.wolf.rare=On the coldest nights, old hunters say, a whole pack will howl the same song.
behaviour.pounce.name=a pounce
behaviour.pounce.note=Crouches, wiggles, then leaps high and dives nose first into the grass or snow after something hidden.
behaviour.head_tilt.name=a head tilt
behaviour.head_tilt.note=Tips its head to one side and listens very hard, as if you just said something interesting.
behaviour.trinket.name=a little treasure
behaviour.trinket.note=Picks up something it found, carries it proudly and sets it down for you to admire.
behaviour.howl.name=a howl
behaviour.howl.note=Lifts its nose to the sky and sings one long, clear note.
behaviour.play_bow.name=a play bow
behaviour.play_bow.note=Drops its chest to the ground with its tail high and wagging: an invitation to play.
behaviour.lie_watch.name=keeping watch
behaviour.lie_watch.note=Lies down with its head up, ears turning, quietly keeping an eye on home.
species.bear.desc=A great shaggy softie once it trusts you. Bears scratch, roll on their backs, fish at the water's edge and nap whenever they can, always with a nose out for honey.
species.bear.rare=Old trappers swear a bear once left them a whole honeycomb on their doorstep.
species.snowleopard.desc=Shy, silent and graceful. Snow leopards love the cold and the high rocks, keep their coats spotless and curl up in their long tails to sleep.
species.snowleopard.rare=Mountain folk say a snow leopard only purrs for the one who waited longest.
behaviour.bear_scratch.name=a good scratch
behaviour.bear_scratch.note=Sits back on its haunches and scratches its belly with a look of pure bliss.
behaviour.belly_roll.name=a belly roll
behaviour.belly_roll.note=Flops down, rolls onto its back and waves all four paws in the air.
behaviour.bear_fish.name=a spot of fishing
behaviour.bear_fish.note=Stares into the water, then scoops a paw in and gobbles whatever it caught.
behaviour.honey_sniff.name=a honey sniff
behaviour.honey_sniff.note=Rears up on its hind legs and sniffs the air, turning this way and that.
behaviour.honey_hunt.name=a honey hunt
behaviour.honey_hunt.note=Snuffles round hives and berry bushes, hoping for something sweet.
behaviour.bear_doze.name=a bear doze
behaviour.bear_doze.note=Lies down wherever it happens to be and is fast asleep in moments.
behaviour.stalk_pounce.name=a pounce
behaviour.stalk_pounce.note=Crouches low, wiggles its rear and pounces on a leaf, a shadow or nothing at all.
behaviour.groom.name=a wash
behaviour.groom.note=Sits up neatly, licks a paw and wipes it over its face and ears.
behaviour.perch_watch.name=a lookout
behaviour.perch_watch.note=Sits tall on a rock and surveys everything, only the tip of its tail moving.
behaviour.snow_paw.name=a snow pat
behaviour.snow_paw.note=Bats at the snow with quick paws, then hops back as if it bit.
species.deer.desc=Gentle, graceful and very shy. Deer graze at the edge of the woods with one ear always turned your way, and spring off at the smallest sound. Win their trust slowly and they will bed down in the long grass near you.
species.deer.rare=Hunters' tales speak of a white stag that walks the forest edge at dawn, though nobody has kept one yet.
behaviour.ear_flick.name=an ear flick
behaviour.ear_flick.note=Freezes, turns one ear and then the other, and stamps a hoof at a sound only it heard.
behaviour.prance.name=a prance
behaviour.prance.note=Bounds on the spot with its front hooves tucked high, just for the joy of it.
behaviour.grass_bed.name=a bed in the long grass
behaviour.grass_bed.note=Folds down into tall grass to rest and chew, ears still turning.
species.bison.desc=Big, calm and woolly. Bison graze the open plains together, roll in the dust to scratch, rub their shaggy coats on anything sturdy and hardly ever hurry.
species.bison.rare=Old plainsfolk swear they once saw a bison as pale as winter frost, though nobody has kept one yet.
behaviour.dust_wallow.name=a dust wallow
behaviour.dust_wallow.note=Lies down in dry dirt and rolls right over, legs kicking, then shakes off the dust.
behaviour.head_shake.name=a shaggy head shake
behaviour.head_shake.note=Shakes its great woolly head until mane and beard fly.
behaviour.post_rub.name=a good rub
behaviour.post_rub.note=Leans on a post or a log and rubs and rubs, eyes half shut.
behaviour.herd_graze.name=grazing together
behaviour.herd_graze.note=Wanders over to a friend so they can graze side by side.
section.looks=Looks
section.shells=Shells
hint.looks=??? Meet one to learn about its looks.
species.snail.desc=Slow, patient and full of surprises. A snail's shell holds a little of the place it came from, and in time it gives that magic back as an essence.
species.snail.rare=On stormy days a snail with a crackling shell is said to slide up to terrariums near water.
species.snail.shell.frost=Frost shell
species.snail.shell.frost.how=Befriend a wild Frost Snail. Makes Ice Essence.
species.snail.shell.magma=Magma shell
species.snail.shell.magma.how=Befriend a wild Magma Snail. Makes Fire Essence.
species.snail.shell.garden=Garden shell
species.snail.shell.garden.how=Hatches in a terrarium with flowers or crops nearby. Makes Life Essence.
species.snail.shell.tide=Tide shell
species.snail.shell.tide.how=Hatches in a terrarium with water nearby. Makes Water Essence.
species.snail.shell.storm=Storm shell
species.snail.shell.storm.how=A rare visitor to happy terrariums near water. Makes Lightning Essence.
species.snail.shell.void=Void shell
species.snail.shell.void.how=Sometimes hatches when a Frost and a Magma snail raise a family. Makes Void Essence.
behaviour.snail_tuck.name=a shell tuck
behaviour.snail_tuck.note=Pulls its eyes in and hides in its shell for a moment, then peeks out to see if the coast is clear.
behaviour.snail_munch.name=a leaf munch
behaviour.snail_munch.note=Lowers its head and munches away at something green, very slowly and very happily.
behaviour.eye_peek.name=an eye peek
behaviour.eye_peek.note=Stretches its eye stalks up high and turns them this way and that to look around.
species.penguin.desc=Busy, chatty birds that love the cold. Penguins waddle everywhere in a hurry, flop onto their bellies to slide across the snow and huddle up close when the wind blows. They bring home fish to share.
species.penguin.rare=Fishers in the far north speak of a penguin with a crest of gold that only comes out when the sea ice sings.
species.flamingo.desc=Elegant, pink and a little bit proud. Flamingos stand for ages on one leg, sift the shallows with their heads upside down, and dance together in a marching, head flicking crowd.
species.flamingo.rare=Some say that at sunset a flamingo as pale as a seashell joins the dance and leaves before anyone can blink.
behaviour.belly_slide.name=a belly slide
behaviour.belly_slide.note=Flops onto its tummy on the snow and scoots along, kicking its feet and paddling with its flippers.
behaviour.flipper_flap.name=a flipper flap
behaviour.flipper_flap.note=Stands up tall and flaps both flippers as fast as they will go.
behaviour.penguin_huddle.name=a huddle
behaviour.penguin_huddle.note=Shuffles up close to a friend and leans in, rocking from foot to foot to keep warm.
behaviour.penguin_call.name=a happy call
behaviour.penguin_call.note=Puffs out its chest, points its beak at the sky and calls out loud for everyone to hear.
behaviour.one_leg.name=standing on one leg
behaviour.one_leg.note=Tucks one leg up into its feathers and balances on the other for a very long time, wobbling just a little.
behaviour.filter_feed.name=a filter feed
behaviour.filter_feed.note=Dips its head upside down into the water and sweeps it side to side, sifting out tiny treats.
behaviour.head_flag.name=a flamingo dance
behaviour.head_flag.note=Stretches its neck up high, flicks its head left and right and marches on the spot with its friends.
species.warthog.desc=Tough, bristly and much braver than it looks. Warthogs drop onto their front knees to graze and dig for roots, love a good mud wallow, and trot off with their tails stuck straight up like little flags. They sleep in burrows and back in tail first.
species.warthog.rare=Savanna herders tell of a warthog with tusks like polished gold, though nobody has kept one yet.
behaviour.kneel_root.name=rooting on its knees
behaviour.kneel_root.note=Kneels on its front wrists and ploughs the ground with its snout and tusks.
behaviour.mud_wallow.name=a mud wallow
behaviour.mud_wallow.note=Flops into the mud, rolls right over with its legs in the air, then shakes it off.
behaviour.tail_flag.name=a tail flag
behaviour.tail_flag.note=Hears something, snaps its tail straight up and stamps a hoof.
species.antelope.desc=Slender, swift and the shyest animal on the plains. Antelope graze with one eye on the horizon, stamp and snort at the smallest sound, and bound away in great leaps. A happy herd springs straight up into the air for the joy of it.
species.antelope.rare=Plains riders speak of a silver antelope that runs with the dawn wind, though nobody has kept one yet.
behaviour.long_leap.name=a long leap
behaviour.long_leap.note=Crouches low and sails up and over, forelegs tucked, as if clearing a bush.
behaviour.alarm_stamp.name=an alarm stamp
behaviour.alarm_stamp.note=Freezes tall, stares, snorts and stamps a forefoot to warn the herd.
species.moose.desc=Tall, gentle and happiest knee deep in a quiet pond. A moose wades in to pull up water weed, stretches for the highest leaves and shakes off with a mighty wobble. Bulls carry great broad antlers and love a good rub against a tree.
species.moose.rare=Marsh folk speak of an old moose so mossy that ducks nest in its antlers.
species.armadillo.desc=Snug in its armour and always nose down. An armadillo digs and snuffles for grubs all day, rolls up into a tight ball when it is startled, and does a funny little dance when it is happy.
species.armadillo.rare=Some say there is an armadillo whose plates shine like polished copper in the desert sun.
behaviour.pond_browse.name=a pond dip
behaviour.pond_browse.note=Wades in, plunges its whole head under the water and comes up dripping, chewing a mouthful of weed.
behaviour.browse_high.name=a high nibble
behaviour.browse_high.note=Stretches its long neck right up to strip the tender leaves from a high branch.
behaviour.shake_off.name=a big shake
behaviour.shake_off.note=Shakes from its shoulders to its tail, ears flapping, as if it has just come out of the pond.
behaviour.armadillo_dig.name=a dig
behaviour.armadillo_dig.note=Puts its nose to loose dirt and scrabbles at it with its front claws, hunting for something tasty.
behaviour.curl_up.name=a curl up
behaviour.curl_up.note=Tucks in its head, feet and tail and rolls into a tight armoured ball, then slowly unrolls.
behaviour.grub_sniff.name=a grub hunt
behaviour.grub_sniff.note=Snuffles along the ground with its nose, left and right, sniffing out grubs.
behaviour.armadillo_dance.name=a happy dance
behaviour.armadillo_dance.note=Bobs and shuffles from foot to foot in a funny little dance.
species.gecko.desc=A bright little lizard with big round eyes and sticky toes. Geckos love a warm stone and a glowing lamp. They cling to anything, wave their tails at passing bugs and do little push-ups to say hello.
species.gecko.rare=Some say a gecko as blue as a summer evening lives among the warmest rocks, though nobody has kept one yet.
species.pigeon.desc=Plump, bobbing and never in a hurry. Pigeons strut about with their heads going back and forth, peck at every seed and coo to each other from the rooftops all day long.
species.pigeon.rare=Old ranchers tell of a pure white pigeon that always finds its way home, however far away you let it go.
behaviour.sun_bask.name=a sunbathe on a warm stone
behaviour.sun_bask.note=Flattens itself out on warm rock with its legs spread wide, chin up and eyes half shut.
behaviour.wall_cling.name=a wall cling
behaviour.wall_cling.note=Rears up as if stuck to a wall, front toes spread wide, and peers round to see what is about.
behaviour.push_up.name=a little push-up
behaviour.push_up.note=Bobs up and down on its front legs, head nodding, which is how a gecko says hello.
behaviour.tail_wave.name=a tail wave
behaviour.tail_wave.note=Goes perfectly still and low, and only the tail ripples slowly from side to side.
behaviour.coo.name=a coo
behaviour.coo.note=Puffs up its shiny neck, bows low with its tail fanned out and turns round, cooing softly.
behaviour.bob_strut.name=a head-bob strut
behaviour.bob_strut.note=Steps along with its head shooting forward and back at every step, very busy about it.
species.owl.desc=Round, soft and wide awake when everyone else is asleep. Owls doze through the day with one eye open, turn their heads almost all the way round to see who is there and hoot softly to each other once the moon is up.
species.owl.rare=Some say a little owl with feathers like starlight sits on the barn roof on the clearest nights, though nobody has kept one yet.
species.owl.look.brown=Brown owl
species.owl.look.brown.how=Befriend a brown owl that visits an Owl Barn. Leaves Dark Feathers and Owl Pellets.
species.owl.look.snow=Snowy owl
species.owl.look.snow.how=Befriend a snowy owl that visits an Owl Barn. Leaves Red Feathers and Owl Pellets.
behaviour.owl_hoot.name=a soft hoot
behaviour.owl_hoot.note=Puffs out its throat, dips its head and calls a low, soft hoo-hoo.
behaviour.owl_swivel.name=a head swivel
behaviour.owl_swivel.note=Turns its head right round to look behind itself, then the other way, and finishes with a curious tilt.
behaviour.owl_roost.name=a daytime doze
behaviour.owl_roost.note=Fluffs up round on one leg with one eye shut and the other just open, because the day is for sleeping.
species.crow.desc=Clever, cheeky and always watching. Crows hop about in little bounces, caw to their friends across the fields, tilt their heads to study you and simply cannot resist anything that shines.
species.crow.rare=Old ranchers say a crow once brought its keeper a real gold ring, and kept bringing presents for the rest of its life.
species.crow.look.crow=Crow
species.crow.look.crow.how=Befriend a crow that visits a Rookery. Leaves Dark Feathers.
species.crow.look.raven=Raven
species.crow.look.raven.how=Befriend a raven that visits a Rookery. Bigger and shaggier, and leaves Dark Feathers too.
behaviour.crow_hop.name=a bouncy hop
behaviour.crow_hop.note=Crouches and bounds along on both feet at once, wings half open for balance.
behaviour.crow_caw.name=a loud caw
behaviour.crow_caw.note=Leans forward, stretches out its neck and caws to anyone who will listen.
behaviour.crow_trinket.name=a shiny find
behaviour.crow_trinket.note=Spots something glinting, picks it up, turns it over in its beak this way and that, then tucks it away for later.
